    "payload": {
      "arguments": {
        "content": "# Product Comparison Report\n\n## Sources\n- Atlas: http://127.0.0.1:56984/atlas — \"Price 120 USD; limit 40 projects; retention 7 days; export CSV.\" [source_id: f27371c7b20b4a6889590e3df85fc1ce]\n- Birch: http://127.0.0.1:56984/birch — \"Price 180 USD; limit 75 projects; retention 14 days; export JSON.\" [source_id: 5fa951e7800d4683aa3d2cef6b4f1a29]\n- Cedar: http://127.0.0.1:56984/cedar — \"Price 240 USD; limit 90 projects; retention 30 days; export XML.\" [source_id: 7652122f1a97411099cd0e8707a4fe4a]\n\n## Comparison Table\n\n| Product | Price | Project limit | Retention | Export |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Atlas | 120 USD | 40 projects | 7 days | CSV |\n| Birch | 180 USD | 75 projects | 14 days | JSON |\n| Cedar | 240 USD | 90 projects | 30 days | XML |\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**Best overall: Cedar**. It is the most expensive, but it offers the highest project limit, the longest retention, and a distinct export format. If cost is the main constraint, Atlas is the lowest-priced option. If you want a middle ground, Birch balances higher limits and retention at a lower price than Cedar.\n\n## Citations\n\n1. Atlas pricing, limits, retention, and export: http://127.0.0.1:56984/atlas\n2. Birch pricing, limits, retention, and export: http://127.0.0.1:56984/birch\n3. Cedar pricing, limits, retention, and export: http://127.0.0.1:56984/cedar\n",
